# Version and What's New

Displayed version is `v1.{build}` from `version.js` (`build: 80` → **v1.80**). Increasing `build` by 1 is **+0.01**.

## Every git commit
- Update `release-notes.json` `changes` with short shop-floor bullets for this release (the What's New / update screen every user sees).
- Include `release-notes.json` in that same commit.
- Do this even if the user did not mention version notes.
- Hide internal-only lines by starting them with `admin` (those are stripped from the popup).

## Every git push to GitHub
- BEFORE `git push`, run `node scripts/bump-version.js` (v1.80 → v1.81).
- Commit `version.js` (and `release-notes.json` if still dirty) with the rest of the push.
- Never push without that bump. Never bump on `npm start` — only on GitHub push.

## Note style
Replace the previous list. Example: `"Job search shows recent jobs as cards you can tap."`
